  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;During the three months ended March 31, 2026, pursuant to the Cash Management Agreement among Norco Pipe Line Company, LLC and its affiliates, the Company effected a settlement of its payable from affiliate, Buckeye Pipe Line Holdings, L.P., in the amount of $0.4 million, previously included in Payable from Affiliated Companies, through an increase in its Additional Paid-in-Capital, effectively representing a non-cash capital contribution from Buckeye Pipe Line Holdings, L.P.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
